          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            When
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            are modeled as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
            takes the form of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            between a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sSet-enriched+presheaves"} model structure on sSet-enriched presheaves
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+model+structure"} slice model structure
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            which has been introduced under the name
            %em straightening and unstraightening
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie 2009, Sec. 3.2
          %p
            Concretely, in the notation recalled at
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+quasi-categories+and+simplicial+categories"} relation between quasi-categories and simplicial categories
          %p
            For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℭ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{C}[S] \to C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi St
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi Un
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi St
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (St_\phi\dashv Un_\phi)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  sSet/S \xrightarrow{\;\; St \;\;} [C^{op}, sSet]
          %p
            which (under an assumption on the parameter
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            between
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                equipped with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+right+fibrations"} model structure for right fibrations
                (also called contravariant model structure in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT
            %li
              %p
                the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
                equipped with
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global projective model structure
          %p
            There is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi St
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi Un
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi St
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (St_\phi \dashv Un_\phi)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  sSet^+/S \stackrel{St}{\;\; \longrightarrow \;\;} [C^{op}, sSet^+]
          %p between
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+Cartesian+fibrations"} model structure for Cartesian fibrations
            %li
              %p
                the global projective
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
                with values in the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+marked+simplicial+sets"} model structure on marked simplicial sets
          %p In both cases,
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi St
                        %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} St_\phi
                is called the
                %em straightening functor
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Un
                        %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Un_\phi
                is called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em unstraightening functor
          %p
            These names have been chosen due to the fact that objects in the left hand category are defined by existential assertions and choices where on the right side these properties become
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+laws"} coherence laws
            being part of the structure.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+fibration"} cartesian fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cleavage"} cleavage
          %h2#references References
          %p The original result is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Lurie09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , Sec. 3.2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/titles/8957.html"} pup:8957
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/papers/HTT.pdf"} pdf
          %p Intuition of Lurie’s construction is discussed in:
          %ul
            %li#direct
              MathOverflow:
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/322763"} Why is the straightening functor the analogue of the Grothendieck construction?
          %p Further discussion:
          %ul
            %li#Stevenson15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"}> Danny Stevenson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Covariant Model Structures and Simplicial Localization
                %strong 3
                (2017) 141-202 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1512.04815"}> arXiv:1512.04815
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+Heuts"}> Gijs Heuts
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                %em Left fibrations and homotopy colimits II
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.01274"}> arXiv:1602.01274
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Campbell"}> Alexander Campbell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A modular proof of the straightening theorem
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://acmbl.github.io/straight_slides.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Campbell-ModularProofofStraightening.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabian+Hebestreit"}> Fabian Hebestreit
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+Heuts"} Gijs Heuts
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jaco+Ruit"} Jaco Ruit
                %em A short proof of the straightening theorem
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.00069"}> arXiv:2111.00069
                ).
          %p
            Discussion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+internal+to+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} internal to
            any
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Louis+Martini"}> Louis Martini
              ,
              %em Cocartesian fibrations and straightening internal to an ∞-topos
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.00295"}> arXiv:2204.00295
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion of straightening and unstraightening entirely within the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hoang+Kim+Nguyen"} Hoang Kim Nguyen
              %em The universal coCartesian fibration
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.08945"}> arXiv:2210.08945
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            which (along the lines of the discussion of the universal left fibration from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "universal+coCartesian+fibration#Cisinski19"} Cisinski 2019
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coCartesian+fibration"} universal coCartesian fibration
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+homotopy+type+theory"} directed homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#CisinskiEtAl23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hoang+Kim+Nguyen"} Hoang Kim Nguyen
              = succeed "," do
                %em Univalent Directed Type Theory
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/index.html"} CMU Homotopy Type Theory Seminar
              (13, 20, 27 Mar 2023) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/index.html#230313"}> web
              , video 1:
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5YOltuTcBK8"}> YT
              , 2:
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xWmELBvHMPo"}> YT
              , 3:
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P0Cfb4eUJo4"}> YT
              ; slides 0:
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-intro_talk1.pdf"}> pdf
              , 1:
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-talk1.pdf"}> pdf
              , 2:
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-talk2.pdf"}> pdf
              , 3:
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-talk3.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            (see
            %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/P0Cfb4eUJo4?t=4618"} video 3 at 1:16:58
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/seminars/slides/cisinski-nguyen-walde-talk3.pdf#page=33"} slide 3.33
          %p
            Discussion of straightening and unstraightening for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-categories"} (∞,n)-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lyne+Moser"}> Lyne Moser
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"} Nima Rasekh
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martina+Rovelli"} Martina Rovelli
              %em An (∞,n)-categorical straightening-unstraightening construction
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.07259"}> arXiv:2307.07259
              ).
